The <ansi fg="command">devtool</ansi> command provides admin utilities for building and verifying world content.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

<ansi fg="yellow">ZONE CONSISTENCY CHECKER</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">devtool check [zone]</ansi>
Scans every room YAML in a zone and reports structural problems:
  - Missing reverse exits (e.g. north→2 but room 2 has no south exit)
  - Exits with invalid destination IDs
  - Orphan rooms that nothing else connects to

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool check dogmud</ansi>
  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool check The Arctic</ansi>

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

<ansi fg="yellow">GRID GENERATOR</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">devtool makezone [name] [width] [height]</ansi>
Creates a rectangular grid of rooms in the named zone.  Every adjacent pair
of rooms is automatically connected with bidirectional cardinal exits.

The zone name may contain spaces — width and height are always the last two
arguments.

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool makezone test_grid 3 3</ansi>     → 9 rooms (3 wide × 3 tall)
  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool makezone The Dark Forest 5 10</ansi> → 50 rooms

<ansi fg="red">Note:</ansi> this writes YAML files on disk.  The server must be restarted (or the
zone reloaded) before the new rooms are accessible in-game.  Run
<ansi fg="command">devtool check [name]</ansi> afterwards to confirm the grid is clean.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

<ansi fg="yellow">CROSS-ZONE ROOM LINKER</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">devtool linkzones [zoneA]/[roomIdA] [direction] [zoneB]/[roomIdB]</ansi>
Adds a bidirectional exit between two rooms that may live in different zones.
Both room template files are updated on disk immediately.

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool linkzones startland/1 east test_grid/1000</ansi>
       Adds east→1000 on room 1, and west→1 on room 1000.

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool linkzones dungeon_level_1/50 down dungeon_level_2/51</ansi>

Valid directions: north, south, east, west, northeast, northwest,
                 southeast, southwest, up, down

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

<ansi fg="yellow">JSON API  (for scripting / LLM tool calls)</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">devtool json [json_string]</ansi>
Executes any of the above operations via a JSON request envelope and returns
a JSON response.  Useful for scripting or AI-driven world generation.

Request format:
  { "action": "<ansi fg="command">check</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">makezone</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">linkzones</ansi>", "params": { ... } }

<ansi fg="command">check</ansi>     params: zone
<ansi fg="command">makezone</ansi>  params: name, width, height
<ansi fg="command">linkzones</ansi> params: zone_a, room_a, direction, zone_b, room_b

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool json {"action":"check","params":{"zone":"test_grid"}}</ansi>
  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool json {"action":"makezone","params":{"name":"cave_system","width":4,"height":4}}</ansi>
  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool json {"action":"linkzones","params":{"zone_a":"startland","room_a":1,"direction":"east","zone_b":"test_grid","room_b":1000}}</ansi>

Response format:
  { "success": true, "action": "...", "result": { ... } }
  { "success": false, "action": "...", "error": "..." }

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

<ansi fg="yellow">FOLD PRESSURE DIAGNOSTICS</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">devtool pressure</ansi>
Reports the current Fold pressure (0.0–1.0) and each Witness moon's
contribution to it.  Also shows tonight's fold ceiling.

  e.g. <ansi fg="command">devtool pressure</ansi>

Fold pressure 0.0 = all moons at new moon (minimum spell complexity allowed)
Fold pressure 1.0 = all moons at full moon (maximum spell complexity allowed)
Fold ceiling   4  = only spells requiring ≤4 folds can be initiated
Fold ceiling   8  = spells requiring up to 8 folds can be initiated

JSON API: <ansi fg="command">devtool json {"action":"pressure","params":{}}</ansi>
